      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We report a case of simultaneous right and left coronary occlusion during percutaneous coronary intervention in the right coronary artery. An aortocoronary dissection induced by the forceful manipulation extended from the right to left sinus of Valsalva and occluded the ostia of both coronary arteries. The patient suffered cardiogenic shock and ventricular fibrillation. However, after successful rapid stenting to right and left coronary arteries, safe discharge was possible."},
